      <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Tall users get disproportionate lower back pain from two structural mismatches: (1) lumbar support positioned too low (designed for users up to ~6'1"), leaving the lumbar unsupported; (2) seat height too low, tilting the pelvis posteriorly and flattening the lumbar curve. The fix is a chair with adjustable lumbar height reaching 10"–12" above the seat pan and a seat height ceiling of 21"+ depending on your height. The Steelcase Gesture and Leap Plus are the chairs that address both.</p>
